module

public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Galois.Basic
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RootsOfUnity.Basic

import Mathlib.FieldTheory.PurelyInseparable.Basic

/-!
# Galois characters and degrees of finite multiradical extensions

Source: Stacks Project, Fields, Tag 09I6, section Kummer extensions, opening paragraph,
extended from one root to a finite list
(blueprint: lem-sfb-multiradical-galois-degree).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace IntermediateField

/-- Adjoining finitely many n-th roots of nonzero elements, with n invertible and all
n-th roots of unity in the base, gives a finite Galois extension. Its Kummer character
is injective and its degree divides n to the number of generators. The coordinate
formula is read in the fixed algebraic closure; it uniquely specifies the character.

Source: Stacks Project, Fields, Tag 09I6, section Kummer extensions, opening paragraph,
in its finite-list product-character form
(blueprint: lem-sfb-multiradical-galois-degree).

Proof:
1. For r = 0, adjoining the empty range gives the base field. Both automorphism and
   character groups are trivial, and the degree is 1, dividing n^0.
2. Each X^n - a is separable: its derivative is n X^(n-1), and the Bezout identity
   -a^(-1)(X^n-a) + (na)^(-1) X (X^n-a)' = 1 applies since n and a are units.
   In particular every chosen radical is nonzero. No irreducibility is needed.
3. Each radical lies in separableClosure F Ω, by the separable-root criterion.
   This is a separable intermediate field, by
   lem-weil-pbc-separable-first-purely-inseparable and
   def-weil-pbc-relative-separable-closure. Hence the field generated by the radicals
   is separable over F; the minimal polynomials agree under the field inclusion.
4. By lem-pc-separable-polynomial-distinct-roots-alg-closed, X^n - 1 has n distinct
   roots in Ω. The splitting hypothesis puts all of them in F, so they are exactly
   rootsOfUnity n F, which therefore has n elements.
5. Scaling this factorization by each radical shows that X^n - a_j splits over the
   generated field, with roots α_j ζ. For r > 0 the product of these binomials is
   nonconstant, splits, and its roots generate exactly the same field. Thus
   lem-sfb-splitting-field-finite-normal gives finite dimensionality and normality.
   Together with step 3 this is Galois. The product need not be separable.
6. The ratio σ(α_j)/α_j has n-th power 1. Step 4 gives its unique descent to
   rootsOfUnity n F. These scalars are fixed by σ, so the ratios multiply under
   composition of automorphisms and give the stated group homomorphism.
7. Equal characters imply agreement on every radical. The agreement set of two
   F-automorphisms is a subfield containing F and the radicals, hence the entire
   generated field. This proves injectivity.
8. By lem-weil-pbc-finite-galois-fixed-field, the finite automorphism group has order
   equal to the field degree. Its character target has order n^r by step 4.
9. Let I be the image of the character and choose one representative of each coset
   of I in the finite target. Multiplication gives a bijection from representatives
   times the automorphism group to the target: existence follows from coset
   membership, uniqueness from cancellation and injectivity. Counting gives
   n^r = (number of representatives) times the degree, proving divisibility. -/
theorem multiradical_galois_degree
    (F : Type u) [Field F] (Ω : Type v) [Field Ω] [Algebra F Ω] [IsAlgClosure F Ω]
    (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (hnF : IsUnit (n : F))
    (hsplit : (Polynomial.X ^ n - 1 : Polynomial F).Splits)
    (r : ℕ) (a : Fin r → Fˣ) (α : Fin r → Ω)
    (hα : ∀ j : Fin r, α j ^ n = algebraMap F Ω (a j : F)) :
    FiniteDimensional F (adjoin F (Set.range α)) ∧
      IsGalois F (adjoin F (Set.range α)) ∧
      (∃ χ : (adjoin F (Set.range α) ≃ₐ[F] adjoin F (Set.range α)) →*
          (Fin r → rootsOfUnity n F),
        Function.Injective χ ∧
          ∀ (σ : adjoin F (Set.range α) ≃ₐ[F] adjoin F (Set.range α)) (j : Fin r),
            algebraMap F Ω ((χ σ j).val : F) =
              (σ ⟨α j, subset_adjoin F (Set.range α) (Set.mem_range_self j)⟩ : Ω) / α j) ∧
      Module.finrank F (adjoin F (Set.range α)) ∣ n ^ r := by
  sorry

end IntermediateField
